3. **Steps**

**Step 1. Write `skeleton/Skeleton.tsx` exactly:**

```tsx
// #2115, R2115000: the shape of what a menu panel waits for, drawn in place of its "Loading …" line, in
// four variants: a card grid, list rows, table rows and a generic panel. The words stay as a status line
// a screen reader hears and nobody sees; the blocks are aria-hidden. Their shimmer is the one animation,
// left out under Reduce motion, the settings panel's or the OS's (skeleton.css). Presentation only
// (CLAUDE.md rule 7): a fixed number of blank blocks, never a count from the read.

import type { CSSProperties, ReactElement, ReactNode } from "react";

import { useOsReducedMotion } from "../game/useOsReducedMotion.ts";
import { useSetting } from "../settings/store.ts";

import "./skeleton.css";

export type SkeletonVariant = "grid" | "rows" | "table" | "panel";

/** Card tiles: two rows at most in a phone's region, so a skeleton fits one screen (R1581000). */
export const SKELETON_TILES = 8;
/** List rows. */
export const SKELETON_ROWS = 4;
/** Table rows under the header row, and the cells of each. */
export const SKELETON_TABLE_ROWS = 5;
export const SKELETON_TABLE_COLUMNS = 4;
/** A panel's lines under its heading bar. */
export const SKELETON_PANEL_LINES = 2;

export const skeletonTestid = { root: "skeleton", status: "skeleton-status", blocks: "skeleton-blocks" } as const;

export type SkeletonProps = {
  /** What is loading, in the player's words, already through `t()`. */
  label: string;
  variant: SkeletonVariant;
  /** The status line's testid: the one the panel's loading line had. */
  testId?: string;
};

function times(count: number): number[] {
  return Array.from({ length: count }, (_, index) => index);
}

function tableRow(key: string): ReactElement {
  return (
    <span key={key} className="skeleton__table-row">
      {times(SKELETON_TABLE_COLUMNS).map((cell) => (
        <span key={cell} className="skeleton__block skeleton__cell" />
      ))}
    </span>
  );
}

function blocksOf(variant: SkeletonVariant): ReactNode {
  switch (variant) {
    case "grid":
      return times(SKELETON_TILES).map((tile) => <span key={tile} className="skeleton__block skeleton__tile" />);
    case "rows":
      return times(SKELETON_ROWS).map((row) => (
        <span key={row} className="skeleton__row">
          <span className="skeleton__block skeleton__mark" />
          <span className="skeleton__block skeleton__line" />
        </span>
      ));
    case "table":
      return [tableRow("head"), ...times(SKELETON_TABLE_ROWS).map((row) => tableRow(String(row)))];
    case "panel":
      return [
        <span key="title" className="skeleton__block skeleton__title" />,
        ...times(SKELETON_PANEL_LINES).map((line) => <span key={line} className="skeleton__block skeleton__line" />),
      ];
  }
}

export function Skeleton({ label, variant, testId = skeletonTestid.status }: SkeletonProps): ReactElement {
  const panelReduces = useSetting("reduceMotion");
  const osReduces = useOsReducedMotion();
  const reduced = panelReduces || osReduces;
  return (
    <div
      className="skeleton"
      data-testid={skeletonTestid.root}
      data-variant={variant}
      data-motion={reduced ? "reduced" : "full"}
      style={{ "--skeleton-columns": SKELETON_TABLE_COLUMNS } as CSSProperties}
    >
      <p className="skeleton__status" role="status" data-testid={testId}>
        {label}
      </p>
      <div className="skeleton__blocks" aria-hidden="true" data-testid={skeletonTestid.blocks}>
        {blocksOf(variant)}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Step 2. Write `skeleton/skeleton.css`.** Start it with a header comment in the style of `rank/rankCrest.css`. The comment says:
- the blocks take the panel's ink faintly, so they read on dark and light panels alike;
- the root is positioned and clips its content, so its hidden words never reach below the window (`index.css`'s `one-screen__body` note) and R1581000 holds;
- the shimmer is drawn only under full motion.

Do not write the word `animation` followed by `:` inside any comment. Three blocks must appear exactly as written here, because the test matches them after collapsing whitespace:

```css
.skeleton {
  --skeleton-ink: color-mix(in srgb, currentcolor 14%, transparent);
  --skeleton-sheen: color-mix(in srgb, currentcolor 26%, transparent);

  position: relative;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.skeleton__status {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  margin: -1px;
  padding: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip-path: inset(50%);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .skeleton[data-motion="full"] .skeleton__block {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--skeleton-ink) 25%, var(--skeleton-sheen) 50%, var(--skeleton-ink) 75%);
    background-size: 200% 100%;
    animation: skeleton-shimmer 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
}
```

Between `.skeleton__status` and the media block, add these rules, one declaration per line:

| Selector | Declarations |
|---|---|
| `.skeleton__blocks` | `display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding: 4px 0;` |
| `.skeleton__block` | `display: block; min-width: 0; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--skeleton-ink);` |
| `.skeleton[data-variant="grid"] .skeleton__blocks` | `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, var(--card-w)), 1fr)); gap: var(--gap);` |
| `.skeleton__tile` | `aspect-ratio: 82 / 112;` with the comment "a card's: index.css's --card-w by --card-h" |
| `.skeleton__row` | `display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;` |
| `.skeleton__mark` | `flex: none; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%;` |
| `.skeleton__line` | `height: 12px;` |
| `.skeleton__row .skeleton__line` | `flex: 1 1 auto;` |
| `.skeleton__table-row` | `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--skeleton-columns), minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px;` |
| `.skeleton__cell` | `height: 14px;` |
| `.skeleton__table-row:first-child .skeleton__cell` | `height: 10px;` |
| `.skeleton__title` | `width: 40%; height: 18px;` |
| `.skeleton[data-variant="panel"] .skeleton__line:last-child` | `width: 60%;` |

After the media block, add:

```css
@keyframes skeleton-shimmer {
  from { background-position: 100% 0; }
  to { background-position: -100% 0; }
}
```

Expand the `from` and `to` lines in the file's normal style, one declaration per line.

**Step 3. Write `test/skeleton.ts`:**

```ts
// #2115: the check every converted panel's test shares. Test support only; no component imports it.

import { expect } from "vitest";

import { skeletonTestid, type SkeletonVariant } from "../skeleton/Skeleton.tsx";

/** `status` is a panel's loading words: a status line inside a skeleton of `variant`, whose blocks a screen reader skips. */
export function expectSkeleton(status: HTMLElement, variant: SkeletonVariant): void {
  expect(status).toHaveAttribute("role", "status");
  const skeleton = status.closest(`[data-testid="${skeletonTestid.root}"]`);
  expect(skeleton, "the words sit in a skeleton").not.toBeNull();
  expect(skeleton).toHaveAttribute("data-variant", variant);
  const blocks = skeleton?.querySelector(`[data-testid="${skeletonTestid.blocks}"]`);
  expect(blocks).toHaveAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
  expect(blocks?.querySelectorAll(".skeleton__block").length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
}
```

**Step 4. Convert each source in the table.** At each site:
1. Import the component: `import { Skeleton } from "../skeleton/Skeleton.tsx";` (from `main.tsx` the path is `./skeleton/Skeleton.tsx`).
2. Replace the loading `<p …>{t("…")}</p>` with `<Skeleton variant="<variant>" label={t("…")} testId={<testid>} />`. Keep the same `t()` literal, the same condition around it, and the testid from the table. Leave out `testId` where the table names none.
3. Drop the old `<p>`'s classes.

Special cases:
- **`routes/collection.tsx` `Section`:** `<Skeleton variant="rows" label={loading} testId={collectionTestid.loading(part)} />`.
- **`routes/purchases.tsx` `Answered`:** add the prop `skeleton: SkeletonVariant` (a type import) and return `<Skeleton variant={skeleton} label={loading} testId={purchasesTestid.loading(place)} />`. Pass `skeleton="table"` at the card-packs use, `"panel"` at cosmetic-packs and `"rows"` at pity.
- **`routes/stats.tsx`:**
  - the card statistics line: `variant={view === "grid" ? "grid" : "table"}`;
  - "Loading set statistics…": `table`;
  - "Loading players…": `table`;
  - "Loading drill-down data…": `rows`.
- **`stats/CardStatsBlock.tsx`:** keep `<div className="inspect-stats inspect-stats--loading" data-testid={INSPECT_STATS}>` and its title `span`. Replace only the inner `<p>` with a `panel` Skeleton. `routes/almanac.test.tsx` holds that `div`'s node.
- **`practice/DeckPreview.tsx`:** split the branch.
  - When `defsFailed`, keep the `<p className="deck-preview__status">` holding the failure sentence and its `TryAgainButton`, unchanged.
  - Otherwise, render `<div className="deck-preview__status"><Skeleton variant="rows" label={t("Loading the card list…")} /></div>`. The wrapper keeps its `grid-area`.
- **`practice/PracticeSetup.tsx`:** render `{blocked === null ? null : custom.kind === "loading" ? <Skeleton variant="panel" label={blocked} testId={practiceTestid.customBlocked} /> : (the existing <p>)}`.
- **`main.tsx` `Loading`:**
  - Add to `LoadingProps`: `/** #2115: draw a skeleton of this shape, the sentence its hidden status line. */ skeleton?: SkeletonVariant;`.
  - In the body, when `skeleton` is set, render `<Skeleton variant={skeleton} label={t(what)} testId={shellTestid.loading} />` in place of the `<p className="notice shell-panel__loading" …>`.
  - Pass `skeleton="panel"` at the `EngineGate` line (`what="Loading…"`), at the `account.kind === "loading"` line ("Checking your account…") and at the Suspense fallback.

**Step 5. Add the ruling.** Write `spec/rulings/R2115000.md`, with front matter in the format of `spec/rulings/R2035000.md`:
- `id: R2115000`;
- `title: "A menu waiting on a read shows a skeleton of what will arrive, its words kept for a screen reader (issue #2115)"`;
- `cards: "§10.10, R1581000, R200, #2036, #2115"`;
- `proven_in` lists `apps/web/src/skeleton/Skeleton.test.tsx`.

The body says what Step 4 does:
- the four shapes and their fixed counts;
- the hidden status line with the old testid, and the `aria-hidden` blocks;
- no shimmer under either Reduce motion;
- it fits [[R1581000]];
- what is left alone and why;
- "Hearthstone semantics: a menu keeps its frame while its contents load.";
- "Rejected:" a spinner beside the sentence (it says nothing of the shape), counts taken from the read (unknown until it answers), and shimmer under Reduce motion.

Then:
1. Append a paragraph to the end of `spec/11-rulings.md` in the style of its R2035000 paragraph. It opens `**[[R2115000]] draws a skeleton where a menu panel waits on its read (issue #2115, part of #2036, 2026-10-27)**:`, summarizes the ruling in one sentence, and ends "It takes R2115000, the first number of issue #2115's block."
2. Run `cargo jackioh spec index`, then `cargo jackioh spec check`.

**Step 6. Add the README paragraph.** In `apps/web/README.md`, after the paragraph ending "…taller or wider than its allowance." (line 44), add one paragraph that says:
- a menu panel waiting on a read draws `skeleton/Skeleton.tsx` (R2115000) in one of four shapes;
